node_modules
.env
# A BACKUP OF A .env IS STILL A .env. `.env` alone did not match
# `.env.bak-1788575471`, and a `git add -A` at the repo root swept one into a
# commit carrying a live OpenAI key and a GCP service-account key — GitHub's
# push protection refused it, which is the only reason it did not become public
# history. Match every variant, and keep scoping `git add` to paths.
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.sample
*.env.bak*
*.bak-[0-9]*
store-health-ai-dashboard-dist/
client-builds/equimind-gs-engine/.gs-store/
